      "description": "`generators` maps each SED-ML data generator to its terms (`variable`, `coefficient`); a variable is `time`, a\nresult column (an SBML id), or a key of `constants` (constant parameters and compartments). `skip` drops that\nmany leading points (those before the SED-ML output start)."
